  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, $f(x)=a \\sin |x|+b e^{|x|}$\r\nWe know that $\\sin |x|$ and $e^{|x|}$ is not\r\ndifferentiable at $x=0$.\r\nTherefore, for $f(x)$ to differentiable at $x=0$, we\r\nmust have $a=b=0$.\r\n$\\therefore$\r\n$$\r\na+b=0\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
